'''''Diplotaxis erucoides''''', the '''white rocket'''<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> or  '''white wallrocket''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=DIER5|taxon=Diplotaxis erucoides|accessdate=20 January 2016}}</ref> is a species of [[annual plant|annual]] [[herb]] of the family [[Brassicaceae]] native to [[West Mediterranean]].<ref name="Pignatti">{{cite book|first1=Sandro|last1=Pignatti|title=Flora d'Italia|language=it|year=1982|volume=1|pages=466|publisher=Edagricole |isbn=9788850624492}}</ref>

== Description ==
''Diplotaxis erucoides'' is an [[herbaceous plant]] up to {{Convert|20–60|cm|frac=2}} tall, with green, erect [[plant stem|stem]], sparsely [[pubescent (botany)|pubescent]], and [[Glossary of botanical terms#pinnatisect|pinnatisect]] [[leaves]] up to 15&nbsp;cm long. It has [[raceme]]s of white [[flowers]] with four 6–8&nbsp;mm [[petal]]s, four [[sepal]]s, six [[stamen]]s and a [[style (botany)|style]] with green [[stigma (botany)|stigma]]. The [[fruit]] is a 25–33&nbsp;mm [[siliqua (botany)|siliqua]] containing 40–80 [[seeds]] in two parallel series.<ref name="Pignatti" /><ref name="Acta">{{cite web|first1=Giuliano|last1=Salvai|title=Diplotaxis erucoides|year=2008|website=Actaplantarum|url=http://www.actaplantarum.org/floraitaliae/viewtopic.php?f=95&t=7645|accessdate=20 January 2015|archive-date=27 March 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150327045301/http://www.actaplantarum.org/floraitaliae/viewtopic.php?f=95&t=7645|url-status=dead}}</ref>

